Declared dependencies
=====================

A pyproject.toml names these and an installer fetches them. Their code is not
in this repository. The list holds every dependency that is copyleft or that
installs from git rather than PyPI. Every other direct third-party dependency
installs from PyPI under a permissive licence.

bgnorm (bgnormPy)
  Declared: packages/clinicalomx_pipelines/pyproject.toml
  Source:   https://github.com/BhuvaLab/bgnormPy, tag v0.1.2
  Licence:  GPL-3.0. The full text is the LICENSE file in that repository.

  This repository declares bgnorm as a dependency and does not include its
  code, so this repository's own Apache-2.0 licence is unaffected. The bgnorm
  container image, packages/clinicalomx_pipelines/qptiff_pipeline/containers/
  Dockerfile.bgnorm, is built FROM the upstream ghcr.io/bhuvalab/bgnormpy image
  and installs this repository's code on top, so it bundles GPL-3.0 code.
  Publishing that image distributes a combined work, and GPL-3.0 terms attach
  to it.

ultralytics
  Declared: packages/clinicalomx_ml/pyproject.toml, a base dependency of
            clinical-roi
  Source:   PyPI, https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
  Licence:  AGPL-3.0

  The same split applies. The declaration leaves this repository's licence
  unaffected. Every croi image built from packages/clinicalomx_ml/roi_detection/
  containers/ installs ultralytics, so publishing a croi image distributes a
  combined work, and AGPL-3.0 terms attach to it.

psycopg2-binary
  Declared: packages/clinicalomx_ledger/pyproject.toml, the hpc worker, and
            the pg test extras of clinicalomx_markers and clinicalomx_omop
  Source:   PyPI, https://github.com/psycopg/psycopg2
  Licence:  LGPL-3.0-or-later, with an exception for linking OpenSSL.

bioio-qptiff
  Declared: packages/clinicalomx_ml/pyproject.toml, and installed at a pinned
            commit by Dockerfile.qptiff and Dockerfile.extract
  Source:   https://github.com/rtubelleza/bioio-qptiff
  Licence:  BSD-3-Clause. Copyright (c) 2026, Rafael Tubelleza. Portions
            Copyright (c) 2023, Bio IO Devs, also BSD-3-Clause.


